  #block(breakable: false)[
  === Complete Solutions
  #sol-item(1, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The test is whether the verdict needs both texts; if it does, the comparison is doing work.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The grid holds the claim and the two mechanisms, and resolves them into a judgement.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    If the verdict stands without the texts, the middle columns were two summaries standing next to each other.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The stem names a comparison, and a comparison needs a shared ground and a difference.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Effectiveness is a judgement, and a judgement without a criterion is a preference.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The proportion is the answer to “how far”, and one-sided answers cap out at half marks.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The frame forces a shared ground and a real difference into one sentence.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A full answer on one text plus a functional contrast is worth far more than a hollow two-text answer.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It cannot be checked, and it poisons every other quotation in the script.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A described moment can be assessed; an invented line cannot.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Fifty-four seconds includes the reading, which is why a question that has taken ninety seconds must be banked and left.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The first marks are the cheapest, and finding them calms the clock.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Recognition is faster than argument, so the cheap marks are banked before the expensive ones.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    There is no negative marking, so a guess has a one-in-four chance and a blank has none.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Wholesale changes replace considered answers with panic, which is worse than either guessing or checking.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Length is not accuracy, and the qualifying clause is often where the option fails.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The distinctions the paper tests are usually between the options rather than in the stem.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Dialogue and staging are available in one; narration and description in the other, and the comparison must be fair to both.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The shared ground is only the first of three parts; the difference and the verdict are what earn the marks.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A criterion you cannot apply consistently will collapse when the second text is examined.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The verdict must follow the test; a verdict chosen first turns the essay into advocacy.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A stage presents, a narrator reports, and the difference in presentation is often where the comparison lives.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Organising by point keeps the comparison live; organising by text makes two essays and calls the join a comparison.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Concession is the visible proof that the verdict was tested rather than assumed.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A short functional contrast does what the comparison needs without pretending to knowledge you do not have.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Misalignment is the commonest avoidable loss in a CBT-style paper.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Time is a budget, and overspending early is paid for by the questions at the end.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The quotation serves the point; a block quotation with no comment earns nothing.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Judgement needs a claim, an objection and a verdict, none of which fits into ten seconds.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The clock is part of the assessment, so the clock has to be trained along with the content.
  ]

]

